{"skill":{"slug":"context-optimizer","displayName":"Context Optimizer"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769831499415,"changelog":"Initial release of context-optimizer (v1.0.0):\n\n- Advanced context management optimized for DeepSeek’s 64k context window.\n- Auto-compaction with multiple strategies: semantic, temporal, extractive, and adaptive.\n- Dynamic, query-aware context selection using relevance scoring and relevance decay.\n- Hierarchical memory system with context archive for selective long-term storage and retrieval.\n- Real-time context health monitoring and optimization event logging to chat.\n- Flexible configuration options for thresholds, strategies, logging format, and archive behavior.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"chat-logger.js","size":3140,"sha256":"8e92fae8d1f37267e41a67bb59a1d068b3946d9f62d2996298bccb6f12879ea6","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"SUMMARY.md","size":3882,"sha256":"8010e601be23f1bc5a0ae29e36238d9b4f5a8f80fb24e1acfecf1eb0d6216a95","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"INSTALL.md","size":5980,"sha256":"71cb25004db567e6b252caabbcba4ee60d631542ff5fb3ea2fffaf207f5e4d5b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":4333,"sha256":"7cf7a60546dc3d5e988ff9611d310825135348806221e49aed29d1eb3c96023b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"package.json","size":532,"sha256":"0f967e1eeb25edf5beaa8d302cd32123e61e006de0b63823db13a958c4fcdb36","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6381,"sha256":"857163b8eaf7930e5a80c07938fe4983c288645d7cb90e53eadfafeb2dfa52c1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"lib/index.js","size":65358,"sha256":"3919b044396cb6d32edb8502c0e845141733867bb6b5e609bf4b074b9fe72d89","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/cli.js","size":5305,"sha256":"67e10cc1f2ff89d4e41590e3afcbe5c8ad6d06a057322ad6626e223ab2da958e","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"examples/clawdbot-integration.js","size":5792,"sha256":"55c31541e936a627c3f609ce1c7828bf9d285be249e0f77015bf7acf9aefc416","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"examples/simple-integration.js","size":8811,"sha256":"69cf6e9945745ffc58034f0c277d1f594f1f323ba2bb8f95a4bbdb0ca9c6e64f","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2081,"sha256":"0836ba7fc203191cc4af87a37b016065192d7f35227c111d67ed40003b580b49","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789024229935,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"17342cf822f96b7d17c68d88dd566eb5042b6fcecf97226215fad3cfeec7b3a7","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/17342cf822f96b7d17c68d88dd566eb5042b6fcecf97226215fad3cfeec7b3a7","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: context-optimizer\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill 'context-optimizer' is designed for advanced context management, including token counting, semantic analysis via embeddings, and a local archive system. Its dependencies (`tiktoken`, `@xenova/transformers`) and file system operations (`fs.mkdir`, `fs.readFile`, `fs.writeFile`, `fs.unlink` for a local archive) are directly aligned with its stated purpose. The `@xenova/transformers` library performs a justified network call to download ML models locally on first use. Installation instructions in `SKILL.md` and `INSTALL.md` are standard `npm install` commands. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts against the agent with harmful objectives.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160360092},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":31,"checkedAt":1789024229935},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This context-management skill is mostly purpose-aligned, but it creates a persistent memory layer that stores and reintroduces conversation text in ways users should review carefully before installing.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The default archive path stores pruned conversation content as local JSON up to a 100 MB limit, with no visible encryption, restrictive file mode, redaction, consent gate, or retention policy.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation uses npm dependencies with caret ranges and a transformer model resolved by name at runtime; uninstall guidance includes manual rm -rf commands for the skill and archive paths, which are user-directed but should be treated as irreversible deletion steps.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Archived snippets and some compacted summaries are inserted as system-role messages, which can elevate historical user or assistant text into a more privileged prompt position and create stored prompt-injection risk.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistence is enabled by default, removed messages are automatically archived, content excerpts are logged during archival, old archive entries may be deleted automatically, and archive retrieval can automatically affect later prompt construction.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose of pruning, compacting, archiving, and retrieving context is coherent with the code and documentation, but the capability includes high-impact handling of full conversation content rather than only transient token optimization.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with the skill retaining pruned conversation content on disk and possibly reusing it later. Disable archive and chat logging for sensitive work, choose a private archive path, avoid storing secrets in conversations that may be compacted, and verify archive paths before running any uninstall deletion commands.","findings":"[T02] unexpected: Confirmed in artifact/lib/index.js: archived snippets are added back as system messages with high priority; archive retrieval is purpose-related, but the role elevation is not proportionate.\n[T09] expected: Confirmed that conversation content is persisted in plaintext JSON and content prefixes are logged; local archiving is part of the skill's purpose, but the default storage and logging lack safeguards.\n[T08] expected: Confirmed package dependencies use caret ranges and the transformer model is loaded by name; this is expected for semantic search but weakens reproducibility and reviewability.\n[SQP-2] expected: Confirmed automatic archive storage, cleanup, clear behavior, and limited warning language; these are aligned with a context archive but under-disclosed for sensitive conversations.\n[SSD-3] unexpected: Confirmed searchable persisted history and automatic reinjection into live context; retrieval is expected, but automatic system-level reinjection of stored conversation text is a material concern.\n[TM1] expected: Confirmed uninstall documentation includes rm -rf commands. This is a manual uninstall pattern rather than hidden destructive behavior, but users should verify paths and back up archives first.\n[MP3] expected: The example clear methods reset local conversation buffers and stats; this is expected for a context manager and is not by itself malicious memory poisoning.\n[TP4] expected: The scanner's capability-mismatch concern is mostly downgraded: the inspected lib implements archive, dynamic context, relevance scoring, compaction, and logging behavior, though naming between context-optimizer and context-pruner is inconsistent.\n[AE1] expected: Downgraded for final adjudication because artifact/lib/index.js was present in this workspace and inspected directly.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789024229935}}}}}